+# Milk-V Jupiter (SpacemiT K1) with an AMD GPU, modular variant for booting
+# with an initramfs (Debian creates one when the kernel package is installed).
+#
+# Same board support and fixes as k1_amdgpu_defconfig, but drivers that a
+# distribution kernel normally builds as modules are modules here: GPU
+# (amdgpu/radeon/nouveau), sound, media, network (K1 EMAC, PHYs, PCIe/USB
+# cards), storage (MMC/SDHCI-K1, NVMe, SCSI disks, USB storage), USB (DWC3,
+# xHCI, HID, onboard hub), ext4 and other filesystems, netfilter, crypto.
+# The SoC base stays built in: clocks, pinctrl, resets, regulators/PMIC, I2C,
+# GPIO, serial console, PCIe controller and PHYs.
+#
+# Needs an initramfs to mount the root filesystem (ext4 and the MMC driver are
+# modules).  No firmware is built in; the GPU firmware
+# comes from /lib/firmware, e.g. Debian package firmware-amd-graphics.
+#
+# Build:   make ARCH=riscv CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-gnu- k1_amdgpu_modules_defconfig
+#          make ARCH=riscv CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-gnu- -j$(nproc) LOCALVERSION= \
+#               KDEB_PKGVERSION=7.2.0-1 KDEB_CHANGELOG_DIST=trixie DPKG_FLAGS=-d bindeb-pkg
